<PARA INFOID = "T120025K081" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "29Jun2006"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Odometer/Trip Meter</TITLE>
<SPEC ID = "T120025K081X01" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Odometer Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "22%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "77%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Display Range</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>0~999999km</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Minimum Unit</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>1km</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>When Display Overflows</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>Holds at 999999</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Movement</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>LCD (Liquid Crystal Display)</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE></SPEC>
<SPEC ID = "T120025K081X02" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Trip Meter A/B Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "22%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "77%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Display Range</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>0.0~9999.9km</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Minimum Unit</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>0.1km</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>When Display Overflows</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>Returns from 9999.9 to 0.0 and continues accumulating</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Display Reset Operation</PTXT>
<PTXT>("0.0km" displayed)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>Press the odo/trip select switch for approximately 0.8 seconds or more.</PTXT>
<PTXT>→ Measurement starts again from the time of reset.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Movement</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>LCD (Liquid Crystal Display)</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE></SPEC>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The modes are switched by pressing the odo/trip select switch located in the combination meter, and are displayed in the order odometer → trip meter A → trip meter B.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>When the taillights are illuminated, the display switches to rheostat display mode.<XREF     REFID = "S478120025Aa36"/>
</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740166b" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "4.542in" />
</FIGURE>

<MECA ID = "T120025K081K084" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "12Apr2004"     MECATYPE = "ACTUATE" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Odo/Trip Meter Operation</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The meter computer receives the vehicle speed signal (CAN communication) from the skid control computer, calculates the distance traveled data, and displays the distance traveled on the multi-information display.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>When the odo/trip select switch operation signal is input to the meter computer, the display switches odometer → trip meter A → trip meter B → odometer; when the meter computer receives the reset operation signal of the odo/trip select switch, it returns the trip meter distance display to 0.0km.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The odometer data is retained by the meter computer; the odometer value is stored using a non-volatile memory IC<HINTREF     REFID = "H478120025K081K08401"/> and is retained even after the +B power is turned OFF.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<HINT>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT ID = "H478120025K081K08401">A memory IC that continues to retain data even when power is not supplied</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></HINT>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740243b" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "2.958in" /><FIGCAPTION><L ja="コンビネーションメーター">Combination Meter</L><L ja="メーターコンピューター">Meter Computer</L><L ja="CAN通信">CAN communication</L><L ja="電源回路">Power Circuit</L><L ja="スキッドコントロールコンピューター">Skid Control Computer</L><L ja="車速信号">Vehicle speed signal</L><L ja="不揮発性メモリーIC">Non-volatile Memory IC</L><L ja="マルチインフォメーションディスプレイ">Multi-information Display</L><L ja="操作信号">Operation signal</L><L ja="オド／トリップ切り替えスイッチ">Odo/Trip Switch</L></FIGCAPTION>
</FIGURE>
</MECA>
</PARA>
